1
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kick a pebble and it
flies until it gets there.

3
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:29,340
We were talking, to the oak tree by the gym.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
They laughed at me for staying so cheerful.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
Guts, there's only one way.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare, and the unchanging streetscape.

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
Gentler, you know.

9
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing.

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,700
The sun has already set.

11
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:53,880
Are the yakitori really there?

12
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat,

13
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:02,420
from person to person, passed on.

14
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:04,080
The sunset falls.

15
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too, it drops and ends, doesn't it.

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,740
Magazine, I wonder, happiness again.

17
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:14,660
I only realized it after losing it.

18
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm such a fool.

19
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:27,700
Dance! Dance! Dance!

20
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:41,600
Excuse me, Chief.

21
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:44,260
Slow, slow.

22
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:48,740
Quick, quick, quick, quick, slow, turn!

23
00:01:48,740 --> 00:01:52,400
Aaaaah!

24
00:01:53,260 --> 00:01:55,220
No, no, well, that's...

25
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,560
I've been caught

26
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:05,380
Actually, I've been taking
lowrider dance lessons lately.

27
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:08,220
Lowrider dancing, is it?

28
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:11,100
It's way better than I expected.

29
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:14,520
What do you say, Ohara?
Why don't you take lessons with me?

30
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:17,420
I've got my chief's visits to make, so...

31
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:22,120
Come on, come on.
At first, everyone feels a bit hesitant.

32
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:26,000
But once you try it,
you're sure to get hooked.

33
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,960
Do give it a try!

34
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:29,940
Ahaha...

35
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,380
Alright, now everyone pick a partner.

36
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:39,900
Let's start with the waltz
where we left off yesterday.

37
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,460
It's in 3/4 time, got it?

38
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:43,100
Yes.

39
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:46,860
You're a first-timer, right?

40
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,400
Daijiro Ohara?

41
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,440
Y-yes.

42
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:54,580
Your ballroom dance
experience isn't over, is it?

43
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:59,640
Well, I'll prescribe your steps,
so this way, please.

44
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:02,180
Y-yes, t-thank you in advance for your help.

45
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:10,160
Alright, first straighten your back.
The hold goes like this.

46
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,620
Rest your right hand
just below the shoulder.

47
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:15,560
Don't tense up.

48
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,320
Y-yes.

49
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:19,330
The waltz is mostly about turning,

50
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:22,640
and the basic rhythm is counted 1, 2, 3.

51
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:23,920
Y-yeah, I see.

52
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:42,740
Chief Ohara,
you've really improved, haven't you?

53
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:46,280
It's all thanks to your guidance, Teacher.

54
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:49,660
I never imagined life
could hold such enjoyment.

55
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:58,140
What do you say? Why don't you enter the competition too,
Chief Ohara?

56
00:03:58,460 --> 00:03:59,880
M-me?

57
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:03,920
No way, the partner I'd be paired with

58
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:07,480
If it's all right with you,
I'd be happy to help you out.

59
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,980
R-really?

60
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:14,240
Yes, but in return, you must tell
everyone about ballroom dancing.

61
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:15,980
Y-yes, sir.

62
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:20,740
Ballroom dancing?

63
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:22,540
The chief is doing it?

64
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:27,320
That's right. I suppose you could call it
one of the refinements of being an adult.

65
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:30,820
If it's ballroom dancing,
my wife said she'd like to try it too.

66
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:35,680
Is that so? Then let's definitely do it.
Marital harmony is guaranteed!

67
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,420
Is that how it is?

68
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:39,480
I'm into Bon dancing and Awa odori...

69
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:43,000
Nakagawa and Reiko can dance,
of course, right?

70
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:47,320
Yes, we were made to learn as soon
as we could barely stand and walk.

71
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:50,320
I learned it along with ballet, too.

72
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:52,300
These two are special.

73
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:55,560
On average,
they're different from Japanese people.

74
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:59,340
No, when you straighten your back
like this and dance the waltz,

75
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:03,300
somehow you feel like a foreign leading man.

76
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,760
It's a funny thing, isn't it.

77
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:07,780
Maybe I'll give it a try too.

78
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:13,120
Nyahahaha, Terai dancing? Uhehehe.

79
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:19,360
Right. I'm short, so I just can't get
the lead for the underarm turn to work.

80
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,560
I'll teach you.

81
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,000
Dancing, they say.

82
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:28,560
The count for 4/4 time is quick,
slow, slow, starting from a side step.

83
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:31,720
As expected.

84
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,720
You two look great together, both so tall.

85
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:38,600
Also, the sway at the
start of the foxtrot...

86
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,260
In that case...

87
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:43,020
Fools who dance, fools who watch.

88
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:44,400
Same fools.

89
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,280
What are you, a bug?!

90
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:48,460
But what's this ballroom dancing nonsense!

91
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:50,920
There's no way I'm doing that crap!

92
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:56,440
W-what? A prize of ten million yen?

93
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:58,840
That's right. Take a look at this.

94
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:02,520
Chief Ohara was just
handing these out to everyone.

95
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:05,220
I'm in!

96
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:07,680
Absolutely, I'm in too.

97
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:09,980
I'm doing it, Ryotsu.

98
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:11,440
Me too.

99
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:13,280
You two actually plan to enter?

100
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:15,640
Trying to stop me is pointless, Ryotsu.

101
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:17,920
Dancing with that face?

102
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:20,080
What does my face have to do with it?

103
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:24,020
Stop, stop, rethink this stupid idea!

104
00:06:24,020 --> 00:06:27,580
Saying that, you're trying to
cut down on rivals, aren't you?

105
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:28,500
Gulp!

106
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:29,900
Bullseye!

107
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:33,360
You didn't think I'd stay quiet after hearing about ten million yen,
did you?

108
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:35,740
I'm in! I'm doing ballroom dancing too!

109
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,560
Me too...

110
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:40,840
If Naka-chan will be my partner...

111
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:43,000
I see. I can't do it alone.

112
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,920
I need someone to be my partner.

113
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:47,820
What should I do?

114
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:51,420
Nakagawa-san is obviously
going to partner with Reiko-san.

115
00:06:52,260 --> 00:06:54,720
But desperate times call
for desperate measures.

116
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:57,500
Right, at this point anyone will do.

117
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:01,980
I-I already have Jodie.

118
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:04,380
I've got Nana-chan.

119
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:05,800
I see.

120
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,940
Well, I guess it can't be helped,
even with you two.

121
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:17,580
That guy's a bug.

122
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:18,920
Nakagawa-san.

123
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:22,520
Ever since I first laid eyes on you,
I've thought you're the only one for me.

124
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:26,140
Closing my eyes to everything else,

125
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:28,820
let's become partners just for the money.

126
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:30,500
Partner?

127
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:30,700
Fine.

128
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,420
Don't get happy about
being talked to like that!

129
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:35,820
Geez, Chief.

130
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:36,840
Chief.

131
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:41,620
M-me, I...

132
00:07:41,620 --> 00:07:43,900
Chief.

133
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:46,102
Me

134
00:07:46,152 --> 00:07:53,660
Me? Well, I guess it can't be helped.

135
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:56,620
Alright, shall we partner up?

136
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,580
You're a shoujo manga digger!

137
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:04,960
Zuririn will be your partner!

138
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:05,560
Oof!

139
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:09,300
Undeterred by rivals'
schemes and dirty tricks,

140
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:12,660
blooming a magnificent flower
on the dazzling grand stage is

141
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:14,580
Me!

142
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:17,320
Monsters, get back in your hole!

143
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:18,940
That's so mean!

144
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:19,560
Aaaaaah!

145
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:30,520
First, let's have a look at the waltz. Forget the ballroom basics,
the real problem is the partner

146
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:35,940
Rap is Nakagawa, and Honda is Otohime.

147
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:41,440
Volvo is George, and so on and so forth.

148
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:48,580
With Maria away on business, we're in a real bind.
We have to do something, or this won't go anywhere.

149
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,540
There's nothing else after this.

150
00:08:57,820 --> 00:09:05,880
But looking at it like this, the movements are as precise as a machine.
It's like a mannequin moving.

151
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:08,500
A mannequin

152
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,060
Yeah, this might work.

153
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:14,160
This is where my figure-crafting
skills get to shine.

154
00:09:14,760 --> 00:09:15,780
Just watch.

155
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:20,240
It's done!

156
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:26,160
Every joint in its whole
body can be bent freely.

157
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:28,400
Super life-size beauty figure.

158
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:30,020
It's the lowrider dance version.

159
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:31,820
Right, let's get started.

160
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:46,380
Even if I get a damn partner, if I'm
the one moving it, it's the same thing.

161
00:09:51,020 --> 00:09:53,460
That's why I have a favor to ask you,
old man.

162
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:58,080
It's lowrider dance software that turns
all of a pro's moves into data, right?

163
00:09:58,080 --> 00:10:01,440
Yeah, if we install that into my figure,

164
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:05,780
all I'll have to do is hold its
hands and it'll dance on its own.

165
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:08,520
Well, it's not impossible.

166
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,400
Since it's urgent, too.

167
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:12,960
Two million yen should be enough, right?

168
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:16,480
No way! At least this much is necessary!

169
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:18,500
What, 50,000 is fine?

170
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,400
No, no.

171
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:23,580
Fifty hundred yen? That's reasonable.

172
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:26,940
As if! It's 5 million, 5 million.

173
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:33,640
How about 1 million?
What, 1 million? 800 thousand?

174
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:39,380
Why did 8 million go up?
Why are you bringing it down?

175
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:45,400
Come on, give me a little discount.
Then 3 million.

176
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:52,860
One more offer: 4 million,
3.5 million. Deal!

177
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:57,240
But you'd better have it ready for the competition,
no matter what.

178
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,300
Don't worry.

179
00:10:58,300 --> 00:11:02,520
My staff are all the kind who'll be fine,
even if they can't dance.

180
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:08,260
Honestly, what outrageous old geezers.

181
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:23,100
You hid the battery well, didn't you?

182
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:26,920
since I built a panel switch into its waist.

183
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:30,400
It adjusts its movements to match the music.

184
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:31,920
Alright, let's give it a try.

185
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:35,640
Switch on!

186
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:39,780
First, the waltz.

187
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:49,040
Wow, that's amazing!

188
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,040
Yeah!

189
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:51,420
Splendid!

190
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:55,220
Oh?

191
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:56,620
Whoa!

192
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:01,140
Perfect!

193
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:04,520
Of course, of course, just as I thought.

194
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:06,040
Hahahaha!

195
00:12:06,380 --> 00:12:08,560
But there's one problem.

196
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:11,020
The height difference is too big,
it looks weird!

197
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:15,060
I can't give up here!

198
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:18,240
It's for ten million yen.
I'll stretch its legs a bit!

199
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:41,500
I wonder what happened, senpai.

200
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:44,980
I guess they couldn't
find a partner after all.

201
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:48,940
But I don't think Ryo-chan would
give up over something like that.

202
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,840
Thank you all for waiting.

203
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:00,800
You're late, Ryo-chan.

204
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:02,940
Yeah, well, you know.

205
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:05,060
He's really riding high, isn't he.

206
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:08,240
Honestly, he looks smoother than usual.

207
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:10,900
I see.

208
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:15,900
Ladies and gentlemen.

209
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:18,500
Social Dance in Katsushika!

210
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:20,640
Welcome to the D1 Grand Prix!

211
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:25,780
We will now begin the Katsushika
Social Dance Competition.

212
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:29,200
Go for it, Kankichi!

213
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:33,780
Judging will be scored on
technical and artistic evaluations,

214
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:36,480
and the pair with the
highest overall score will win.

215
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:38,880
First, we start with the preliminary round.

216
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:43,900
So the first dance is the waltz

217
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:50,300
Chief Ohara, don't be so stiff.
Just relax and do it the way you always do.

218
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:03,120
Don't accidentally throw
me across the floor, okay?

219
00:14:04,780 --> 00:14:05,780
Probably.

220
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:10,920
Just being like this makes me happy.

221
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:13,460
Bobby, watch out for nosebleeds.

222
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:14,760
I know.

223
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:20,300
It's fine, Bobby.

224
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:24,340
Surprising.

225
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:26,800
Ryo-chan being so calm like that,
who would have thought.

226
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:29,560
It's because his partner is wonderful.

227
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:32,440
Honestly, who is that woman?

228
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:34,980
Well, it's a face we've never seen before,
isn't it?

229
00:14:37,780 --> 00:14:38,140
What a...

230
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:45,320
As long as I don't press the wrong song select button,
this is ours.

231
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:55,220
Damn it,
the real Lovely Bin is right over there.

232
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:02,140
One-two-three-four, one-two-three-four.

233
00:15:05,460 --> 00:15:06,780
Not bad at all.

234
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:12,900
Now, we will announce the pair that
advanced from the preliminary round.

235
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:14,700
Please look at the monitor.

236
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:19,440
My heart's pounding.

237
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:22,960
Oh God.

238
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:27,960
The pair that advanced from the
preliminary round is this pair!

239
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:39,700
So we didn't make it, then?

240
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:41,180
How disappointing.

241
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:46,200
Damn it,
if only I hadn't gotten a nosebleed.

242
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:48,120
Don't cry, Bobby.

243
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:54,060
Still, Ryotsu making it
through the preliminaries...

244
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:59,640
Of course. His skill is on
a different level from yours.

245
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:02,040
It's annoying,
but I guess it can't be helped.

246
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:04,740
And it's dynamic as well as graceful.

247
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:06,060
Indeed.

248
00:16:06,820 --> 00:16:10,200
Still, to get this good
in such a short time...

249
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:11,440
Seriously.

250
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:14,680
Excuse me, but what's your name?

251
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:15,360
Right?

252
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:17,480
Hey, is this the guy?

253
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:19,760
Calling him "this guy" is rude, Ryo-chan.

254
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:23,780
Anyone can see that a wonderful
dance is thanks to the partner.

255
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:25,860
What's with that...?

256
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:28,720
Well, he does have a name...

257
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:33,594
Ryotsu, I wasn't asking you. Pardon me.

258
00:16:33,644 --> 00:16:36,840
Sorry, he's a man with no
manners or common sense.

259
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:37,800
Mm.

260
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:41,240
I'm Ohara. And you?

261
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:45,680
I'm called Odoriko. The Izu Dancer.

262
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:48,800
The Izu Dancer?

263
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:50,096
Well,

264
00:16:50,146 --> 00:16:54,960
what a name! It's as if you
were born to do social dancing.

265
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,000
Really?

266
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,840
S-sorry,
I need to go to the restroom for a moment...

267
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:01,180
Excuse me!

268
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,440
Why is Ryo-chan here too?

269
00:17:06,420 --> 00:17:07,326
Still,

270
00:17:07,376 --> 00:17:10,520
you have the same expression you
always wear when you're dancing.

271
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:12,900
She's a natural-born dancer.

272
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:17,680
I'm going to use the restroom
before the finals, too.

273
00:17:17,730 --> 00:17:19,240
Excuse me.

274
00:17:21,940 --> 00:17:23,620
Anyway, it's the finals.

275
00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:26,400
We have to keep pulling
this off until the very end.

276
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
Sorry about earlier.

277
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:33,860
How did you end up here?

278
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:35,760
Oh no.

279
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:39,760
Sorry, I was just practicing a secret step.

280
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:45,520
That was close.

281
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:47,180
There he is!

282
00:17:47,940 --> 00:17:49,060
Hey, Ryotsu!

283
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:53,380
Well, well, all of you together.
Is something the matter?

284
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:57,080
Well, it's actually a bit embarrassing...

285
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:59,920
We've all become fans.

286
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:01,560
Fans?

287
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:04,300
Not you, the dancer!

288
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:05,700
She was wonderful.

289
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:07,560
Please give us your autograph.

290
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,380
Me too, please.

291
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:10,840
Please!

292
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:14,500
Come on, you can't do that sort of thing.

293
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:17,200
I told you,
you have nothing to do with this.

294
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:19,380
That's right, Ryotsu, stay out of the way!

295
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:21,380
Please, Miss Dancer!

296
00:18:21,380 --> 00:18:23,860
Look, there are all
sorts of circumstances...

297
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:26,580
What's that?

298
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:32,280
Wait, Ryotsu!

299
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:33,860
Dancer-san!

300
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:37,420
Wait up!

301
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:41,340
This way!

302
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:44,960
Dancer-san!

303
00:18:48,820 --> 00:18:51,560
Damn it, just give up already!

304
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:56,000
Okay, this way!

305
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:58,820
Dancer-san!

306
00:18:59,350 --> 00:19:02,040
Dancer-san, Dancer-san!

307
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,520
This took an unexpected turn.

308
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:14,320
Did I make her a bit too pretty?

309
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:21,020
What's wrong, dancer?
Pull yourself together!

310
00:19:24,060 --> 00:19:25,300
Her head's wobbling.

311
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:26,040
Whoa!

312
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:32,780
I messed with it too much!

313
00:19:34,380 --> 00:19:36,120
I saw that!

314
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:38,600
You...!

315
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:44,240
Shōjo Manga Deka

316
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:45,380
It's Lovely Bin.

317
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:49,360
Shōjo Manga Deka? Were you watching that?

318
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:50,823
Of course,

319
00:19:50,873 --> 00:19:54,500
I saw everything with
these round eyes of mine.

320
00:19:55,980 --> 00:19:58,500
That's the end of the plan, then.

321
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:00,860
There's a way.

322
00:20:01,940 --> 00:20:05,860
What I mean is, I'll take that doll's place.

323
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:08,800
You don't get to say no!

324
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:12,840
Guririn will do his best, Coach.

325
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:15,500
W-why am I the coach?

326
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:19,060
A shoujo manga always needs a coach,
doesn't it?

327
00:20:19,060 --> 00:20:20,620
Well, I suppose so.

328
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:23,360
Either way, you have no choice.

329
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:25,720
You'll make me your partner.

330
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:29,280
Eh, come on, we've come this far.

331
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:31,100
I'll see it through to the end!

332
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:33,160
Aiming for 10 million!

333
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:36,900
And now, the final round is about to begin!

334
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:41,080
The finals demand even
more advanced technique

335
00:20:41,080 --> 00:20:43,080
and artistic expression
than in the preliminaries.

336
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,660
So, which pair will take the championship?

337
00:20:48,420 --> 00:20:50,140
Where is that dancer?

338
00:20:56,020 --> 00:20:57,200
Maybe I'm imagining things.

339
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:00,840
She looks different from before.

340
00:21:05,960 --> 00:21:06,760
Uh-oh.

341
00:21:06,760 --> 00:21:08,080
We've got to do something.

342
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:12,660
If it comes to that,
I'll force my way through.

343
00:21:12,660 --> 00:21:13,800
I'll knock them all out of the way.

344
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:22,420
What's going on here?

345
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:24,080
Pair number 32.

346
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:25,620
That's a big deduction.

347
00:21:27,060 --> 00:21:27,760
Are you all right?

348
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:30,340
It's Ryo-chan, isn't it?

349
00:21:30,340 --> 00:21:31,860
It's Bin!

350
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:36,800
I won't stop at anything
to win the championship.

351
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:38,720
As despicable as ever

352
00:21:43,540 --> 00:21:44,260
Next...

353
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:51,700
The dancing is too dynamic.

354
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:58,440
Whoops, pair number 55 has fallen too!

355
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:00,680
It's Ryotsu, damn him!

356
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:01,880
Excuse me!

357
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:03,720
Found it!

358
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:04,980
Sorry, coming through!

359
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:06,920
What's going on here!

360
00:22:07,060 --> 00:22:09,420
People are falling left and right!

361
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:12,860
Damn you, Ryotsu! I can't forgive you!

362
00:22:13,340 --> 00:22:14,000
Yaaah!

363
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,040
What are you doing, Ryo-chan!

364
00:22:25,460 --> 00:22:26,900
Stop it!

365
00:22:28,220 --> 00:22:30,140
What's with that face?

366
00:22:30,540 --> 00:22:31,200
Ooh, no!

367
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:32,620
Wait, wait, wait!

368
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:35,540
Damn it, you've done it now!

369
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:38,320
Whoa, my legs are wobbling!

370
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:40,540
I'm all dizzy!

371
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,260
That's not good!

372
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:47,880
What are you doing!

373
00:22:49,100 --> 00:22:51,120
This is turning into a real disaster!

374
00:23:20,880 --> 00:23:23,700
Aaaaaah!

375
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:24,240
Karakichi!

376
00:23:33,760 --> 00:23:35,660
Is this the only part-time job there is?

377
00:23:35,660 --> 00:23:37,460
We're not a good fit, are we?

378
00:23:38,180 --> 00:23:39,320
A perfect fit!

379
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:40,720
Stop it, you monster!

380
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:41,680
Help me!

381
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:42,780
Lovey-dovey!

382
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:13,980
I crumpled up boredom like a
incident report and tossed it away.

383
00:24:15,020 --> 00:24:17,460
Bare instincts, exposed instincts.

384
00:24:17,460 --> 00:24:18,500
Become a fool,

385
00:24:19,380 --> 00:24:22,280
reckless and broke, what's wrong with that?

386
00:24:23,840 --> 00:24:27,980
I'll do it my way,
just doing whatever I please.

387
00:24:27,980 --> 00:24:32,600
Chief Ohara's thunder, smoke from his head.

388
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:35,980
Run away and you'll be
caught like a tortoise.

389
00:24:35,980 --> 00:24:37,380
Well, isn't that wonderful.

390
00:24:37,380 --> 00:24:38,240
Oho!

391
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:39,840
In the flowery Edo,

392
00:24:39,840 --> 00:24:40,540
Hey there!

393
00:24:40,540 --> 00:24:41,860
Cool mountain, mighty wind.

394
00:24:41,860 --> 00:24:42,960
Always obliged!

395
00:24:42,960 --> 00:24:45,520
Raging storm!

396
00:24:45,520 --> 00:24:47,500
Maybe the play, nine times over.

397
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:49,020
Jugemu jugemu.

398
00:24:49,020 --> 00:24:50,220
Running out of water here.

399
00:24:50,220 --> 00:24:51,300
Great difference, like fish and water.

400
00:24:51,300 --> 00:24:52,780
Fish and water, cross.

401
00:24:52,780 --> 00:24:53,760
Schools of fish, cross.

402
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:54,520
Fly, cross.

403
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:55,760
Goodbye, to this place.

404
00:24:55,760 --> 00:24:56,400
Right here.

405
00:24:56,920 --> 00:24:58,060
Yabura-kōji

406
00:24:58,060 --> 00:24:58,800
Bura-kōji

407
00:24:58,800 --> 00:24:59,660
Paipo paipo

408
00:24:59,660 --> 00:25:00,220
Paipo no

409
00:25:00,220 --> 00:25:01,120
Shūringan

410
00:25:01,120 --> 00:25:02,200
Shūringan to

411
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:03,080
Gūrindai

412
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:04,300
Gūrindai no

413
00:25:04,300 --> 00:25:05,340
Ponpokopī no

414
00:25:05,340 --> 00:25:06,280
Ponpokonādo

415
00:25:14,840 --> 00:25:17,960
We've just made a huge invention
that'll make the whole world gasp!

416
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:20,180
Isn't it amazing

417
00:25:20,180 --> 00:25:22,720
And I've got more ideas
than I know what to do with.

418
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:25,000
This could make us billionaires,
no doubt about it.

419
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:29,040
Gentlemen, from now on,
call me Doctor Ryotsu.

420
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:32,400
Next time: Inventor King Ryotsu,
see you then.

421
00:25:37,380 --> 00:25:39,100
Surely on camera

422
00:25:39,100 --> 00:25:42,220
Everyone, come on over

423
00:25:42,220 --> 00:25:44,220
To our town

424
00:25:45,060 --> 00:25:45,820
Thank you

